  "articleBody": "Wainscoting can add a ton of character to a room, but a few common missteps can really mess up the look. Let’s talk about how to avoid them! First, don’t skip careful layout planning. Poor layout symmetry or not accounting for outlets, baseboards, and door frames will make the final product look haphazard, not charming. You really want consistent panel spacing, even around obstacles. Second, never install wainscoting directly over uneven walls without correcting them first. This will just amplify the wall’s imperfections and make your wainscoting look wavy. Third, relying solely on small nails or weak adhesive without proper backing or hitting studs is a recipe for disaster; your wainscoting could warp or even detach over time. You need solid support! Lastly, rushing the finishing details, like filling seams or sanding, will show through your final paint or stain job. Take your time for a smooth, professional appearance. If your room has complex angles or you’re aiming for a really precise, built-in look, it might be a good idea to chat with HH Remodeling LLC. We can help you navigate these tricky bits and ensure a beautiful, lasting finish.",
